",null,{"className":"sm:hidden block text-[0.65rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#16A34A]","children":"What it is"}],"The newest terminal: about 97,000 square metres, up to 15 million passengers a year, with a dedicated group check-in area for Hajj and Umrah pilgrims. Phased opening began on 27 September 2026."]}],["$","td","2",{"className":"block sm:table-cell px-4 py-1.5 sm:py-3 leading-relaxed ","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"sm:hidden block text-[0.65rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#16A34A]","children":"Who uses it"}],"Foreign airlines moving from the North Terminal, such as Wizz Air, AJet and SalamAir, plus other carriers as the move continues."]}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"block sm:table-row border-t border-[#16A34A]/10 align-top first:border-t-0 py-2 sm:py-0","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"block sm:table-cell px-4 py-1.5 sm:py-3 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-[#0F172A]","children":[false,"North Terminal"]}],["$","td","1",{"className":"block sm:table-cell px-4 py-1.5 sm:py-3 leading-relaxed ","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"sm:hidden block text-[0.65rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#16A34A]","children":"What it is"}],"The terminal that handled most foreign airlines. Reports say its flights move to Terminal 4 and the Hajj and Umrah Terminals from 17 October 2026."]}],["$","td","2",{"className":"block sm:table-cell px-4 py-1.5 sm:py-3 leading-relaxed ","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"sm:hidden block text-[0.65rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#16A34A]","children":"Who uses it"}],"Being phased out; some tickets may still show it."]}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"block sm:table-row border-t border-[#16A34A]/10 align-top first:border-t-0 py-2 sm:py-0","children":["$L34","$L35","$L36"]}]]}]]}]}]
2b:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 text-xs text-[#6B7280] leading-relaxed max-w-[70ch]","children":"Sources: Khaleej Times (17 October 2026), Gulf News (27 September 2026) and Wego (1 October 2026, updated 2 November 2026). Terminal assignments change; the airline's own booking information is the final word."}]
2c:["$","section","What is Terminal 4 at Jeddah airport?",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-[#0F172A]","children":"What is Terminal 4 at Jeddah airport?"}],[["$","p","0",{"className":"mb-4 leading-[1.8] text-[#475569] max-w-[70ch]","children":"Terminal 4 is the new terminal at King Abdulaziz International Airport, about 97,000 square metres with room for up to 15 million passengers a year. Its phased opening began on 27 September 2026, and it includes a dedicated group check-in area for Hajj and Umrah pilgrims."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"mb-4 leading-[1.8] text-[#475569] max-w-[70ch]","children":"Wizz Air, AJet and SalamAir were the first airlines to move in on 27 September. Fly Jinnah, Nesma Airlines, Akasa Air, SyrianAir, Pegasus, Azerbaijan Airlines and Tunisair followed between 28 September and 3 October. Other airlines are moving gradually as operations allow."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
2d:["$","section","Is the North Terminal at Jeddah airport still used?",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-[#0F172A]","children":"Is the North Terminal at Jeddah airport still used?"}],[["$","p","0",{"className":"mb-4 leading-[1.8] text-[#475569] max-w-[70ch]","children":"The North Terminal is being phased out. Khaleej Times reported on 17 October 2026 that all flights from the North Terminal move to Terminal 4 and the Hajj and Umrah Terminals, effective 17 October."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"mb-4 leading-[1.8] text-[#475569] max-w-[70ch]","children":"Wego reported seven airlines assigned to the Hajj and Umrah Terminal from the North Terminal: Tarco Aviation, Yemenia, SCAT Airlines, Uzbekistan Airways, Daallo Airlines, Somon Air and Sudan Airways. If your ticket says North Terminal, confirm the current terminal with your airline before you book a pickup."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
2e:["$","section","Which Jeddah airport terminal is for Umrah and Hajj flights?",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-[#0F172A]","children":"Which Jeddah airport terminal is for Umrah and Hajj flights?"}],[["$","p","0",{"className":"mb-4 leading-[1.8] text-[#475569] max-w-[70ch]","children":"Pilgrim flights use the Hajj and Umrah Terminal and, since September 2026, Terminal 4, which has its own group check-in area for pilgrims. Many Umrah travellers also arrive through Terminal 1 on scheduled flights, so the terminal depends on the airline, not on the purpose of your trip."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"mb-4 leading-[1.8] text-[#475569] max-w-[70ch]","children":"Jeddah lies inside the Miqat boundary, so pilgrims arriving by air usually enter Ihram on the plane before landing. Our Miqat guide explains the details and what to do if you need the Al-Juhfah Miqat near Rabigh."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
2f:["$","section","How do I meet my driver at Jeddah airport?",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-[#0F172A]","children":"How do I meet my driver at Jeddah airport?"}],[["$","p","0",{"className":"mb-4 leading-[1.8] text-[#475569] max-w-[70ch]","children":"Your driver provides meet and greet at arrivals. Send us your flight number and the terminal your airline shows when you book, and tell us if the terminal changes before you fly."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"mb-4 leading-[1.8] text-[#475569] max-w-[70ch]","children":"We track your flight, so a delay simply moves the pickup to your actual landing time, and 15 to 30 minutes of waiting after landing is free. The terminals are separate buildings, so a message to correct the terminal saves you a long walk or a second transfer."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
30:["$","section","How far is Jeddah airport from Makkah and Madinah?",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-[#0F172A]","children":"How far is Jeddah airport from Makkah and Madinah?"}],[["$","p","0",{"className":"mb-4 leading-[1.8] text-[#475569] max-w-[70ch]","children":"Makkah is about 80 km from Jeddah airport, roughly one hour by road, and Madinah is about 420 km, roughly four to five hours. A private car goes straight from your terminal to your hotel on your schedule, with prayer and rest stops on request."}]],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-[#16A34A]/12 bg-white","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left text-sm","children":[["$","thead",null,{"className":"hidden sm:table-header-group bg-[#FAFAF7] text-[#0F172A]","children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","Option",{"className":"px-4 py-3 font-bold","children":"Option"}],["$","th","Best when",{"className":"px-4 py-3 font-bold","children":"Best when"}],["$","th","Trade-off",{"className":"px-4 py-3 font-bold","children":"Trade-off"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"className":"text-[#475569]","children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"block sm:table-row border-t border-[#16A34A]/10 align-top first:border-t-0 py-2 sm:py-0","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"block sm:table-cell px-4 py-1.5 sm:py-3 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-[#0F172A]","children":[false,"Private car with driver"]}],["$","td","1",{"className":"block sm:table-cell px-4 py-1.5 sm:py-3 leading-relaxed ","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"sm:hidden block text-[0.65rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#16A34A]","children":"Best when"}],"Families, groups, heavy luggage, late-night arrivals, or a hotel that is not beside a station"]}],["$","td","2",{"className":"block sm:table-cell px-4 py-1.5 sm:py-3 leading-relaxed ","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"sm:hidden block text-[0.65rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#16A34A]","children":"Trade-off"}],"Door to door on your schedule; the fare is agreed on WhatsApp before you book"]}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"block sm:table-row border-t border-[#16A34A]/10 align-top first:border-t-0 py-2 sm:py-0","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"block sm:table-cell px-4 py-1.5 sm:py-3 leading-relaxed font-semibold text-[#0F172A]","children":[false,"Haramain high-speed train"]}],["$","td","1",{"className":"block sm:table-cell px-4 py-1.5 sm:py-3 leading-relaxed ","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"sm:hidden block text-[0.65rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#16A34A]","children":"Best when"}],"Light luggage and a hotel close to a station; the Jeddah airport station is connected to Terminal 1, about 45 minutes to Makkah and about 1 hour 45 minutes to Madinah"]}],["$","td","2",{"className":"block sm:table-cell px-4 py-1.5 sm:py-3 leading-relaxed ","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"sm:hidden block text-[0.65rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#16A34A]","children":"Trade-off"}],"Station to station; you arrange the last stretch to your hotel, and a terminal other than Terminal 1 means getting to Terminal 1 first"]}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 text-xs text-[#6B7280] leading-relaxed max-w-[70ch]","children":"Train times from SPA via seo/venues.md. Check the current timetable with the operator."}]]}]
